{
  "order": 2000,
  "name": "Semantic viewer",
  "kind": "module",
  "responsibility": "Reads and explores rendered boards",
  "description": "Reads the board document from the vault of the pane it is drawn in, on the server, or from the talk on a replay, and draws its picture in this page (or asks the server's render route when the page runs no renderer). Owns only camera, selection, view, variant, walkthrough position and drill-down trail, and writes nothing (ADR 0023). A presented walkthrough is one plate over the foot of the picture: a rail of steps, the step's number, heading and words, the keys that step and leave, and at its foot a pill for the voice, which holds the key that narrates while voice is off and what the shell lays over the picture while it is live. The camera keeps the picture clear of the whole plate, and the stage says whether it lays that overlay free over the picture or in the pill, so what is laid there draws itself to fit.",
